# RiskCanvas example environment configuration.
# Copy to ".env" and adjust as needed. ALL values are optional — RiskCanvas
# runs with sensible defaults and requires NO secrets or API keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# --- FastAPI service (riskcanvas/api/app.py) ---
# The bundled `python -m riskcanvas.api.app` entrypoint serves on 127.0.0.1:8004, with
# no auto-reload; these two are all the API reads from the environment:
#   RISKCANVAS_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   RISKCANVAS_PORT=8004
# Under uvicorn directly, choose them with its flags:
#   uvicorn riskcanvas.api.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8004

# --- Market data ---
# Live prices are fetched via yfinance, which needs NO API key.
# yfinance is only used by PortfolioLoader.from_tickers(...) and
# StressTester.estimate_beta(...). An API request that carries `returns` runs
# FULLY OFFLINE (the dashboard sends synthetic per-asset returns and the
# engine computes everything with numpy/scipy, NO network); one without
# `returns` fetches prices — and SPY, for the stress beta — via yfinance.

# --- Frontend (frontend/) ---
# The Next.js dashboard reads NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, inlined at BUILD time, to
# reach the real engine. Unset: `next dev` uses http://localhost:8004, a
# production build calls no engine and shows in-browser demo data. If the
# configured backend is unreachable the UI also falls back to demo data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8004

# The site's public origin, for absolute og:image / twitter:image URLs (build
# time). Unset: `next dev` uses http://localhost:3004; a production build
# ships no preview image rather than a localhost one.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://riskcanvas.example
